// Template for `Config/Secrets.xcconfig`, which is gitignored and must never be
// committed. Copy this file, then paste the real key in place of the
// placeholder:
//
//     cp Config/Secrets.xcconfig.example Config/Secrets.xcconfig
//
// The real key lives outside the repository, in `~/.kamome/routing.env`
// (mode 600), as `GEOAPIFY_API_KEY=…`. To generate this file from it:
//
//     printf 'KAMOME_ROUTING_API_KEY = %s\n' \
//       "$(grep GEOAPIFY_API_KEY ~/.kamome/routing.env | cut -d= -f2-)" \
//       > Config/Secrets.xcconfig
//
// ⚠️ **This keeps the key out of git. It does NOT keep it out of the IPA** —
// it lands in `Info.plist`, and anyone who unpacks a shipped build can read it.
// That is knowingly accepted while Kamome runs on a handful of phones, and it is
// why `Docs/pre-launch.md` blocks submission on moving the key behind a
// no-log Cloudflare Worker. Do not add effort here to defend the binary;
// provider-side key restriction cannot substitute, for the reasons that document
// gives.
//
// Leaving the placeholder in place is treated as "no key" by the app, so a copy
// you forget to edit disables routing rather than sending a bad key.
KAMOME_ROUTING_API_KEY = replace-me-with-the-routing-provider-key
